x86_64-linux  the only names that differ are std::initializer_list<T>::begin/end. clang compiles against libc++'s own std::initializer_list, whose members carry an abi_tag (B9nqe210106) this compiler does not; and under the cross-target invocation clang cannot find <initializer_list> at all, since that header ships with the host libc++ rather than with cxx1. cxx1 builds against include/initializer_list, a plain class template with the same layout. What the case is about - the language step that builds a list from a brace-init and selects the constructor - is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
